  "lectures": [
    {
      "id": "44115826",
      "title": "Two-Way Binding: Repetition",
      "lectureOrder": 147,
      "videoOrder": 139,
      "sourceHash": "6c097a783c6151af4d081fb39074aee0e8f2fa68a53210ecc65db0c0067395e8",
      "cues": [
        {
          "id": 1,
          "start": 0.51,
          "end": 2.34,
          "en": "Now with all that",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 2,
          "start": 2.34,
          "end": 5.299,
          "en": "and with all that usage of inputs and outputs,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 3,
          "start": 5.299,
          "end": 8.179,
          "en": "I'll go back to that new ticket component",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 4,
          "start": 8.179,
          "end": 12.09,
          "en": "and I wanna revisit the approach we're using",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 5,
          "start": 12.09,
          "end": 15.9,
          "en": "for extracting the entered input data.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 6,
          "start": 15.9,
          "end": 20.46,
          "en": "I'm currently doing this with template variables like this",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 7,
          "start": 20.46,
          "end": 22.98,
          "en": "and that approach is absolutely fine, of course.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 8,
          "start": 22.98,
          "end": 27.117,
          "en": "It works fine and there is no reason to change it here.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 9,
          "start": 27.117,
          "end": 32.1,
          "en": "But earlier in the course you learned about two-way binding",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 10,
          "start": 32.1,
          "end": 33.99,
          "en": "and I wanna revisit this here",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 11,
          "start": 33.99,
          "end": 35.82,
          "en": "and then also show you",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 12,
          "start": 35.82,
          "end": 39.63,
          "en": "how you can make your own Components two-way bindable,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 13,
          "start": 39.63,
          "end": 42.57,
          "en": "which is something we haven't done before.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 14,
          "start": 42.57,
          "end": 46.29,
          "en": "But let's start by revisiting two-way binding",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 15,
          "start": 46.29,
          "end": 48.39,
          "en": "on input elements.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 16,
          "start": 48.39,
          "end": 50.55,
          "en": "As you learned earlier in the course,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 17,
          "start": 50.55,
          "end": 53.52,
          "en": "you can use the special NG model directive,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 18,
          "start": 53.52,
          "end": 54.66,
          "en": "which is unlocked",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 19,
          "start": 54.66,
          "end": 59.66,
          "en": "by the forms module to two-way bind input elements",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 20,
          "start": 59.97,
          "end": 64.616,
          "en": "or related elements, so text area elements and so on.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 21,
          "start": 64.616,
          "end": 68.43,
          "en": "And we can use this here in the new ticket Component",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 22,
          "start": 68.43,
          "end": 71.67,
          "en": "to add some new properties that should be managed",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 23,
          "start": 71.67,
          "end": 73.59,
          "en": "with help of two-way binding.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 24,
          "start": 73.59,
          "end": 78.33,
          "en": "And you can either use signals or non-signal properties",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 25,
          "start": 78.33,
          "end": 80.67,
          "en": "as you also saw before in the course.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 26,
          "start": 80.67,
          "end": 85.02,
          "en": "And here I'll start with non-signal properties.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 27,
          "start": 85.02,
          "end": 88.2,
          "en": "So I will add a entered title property,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 28,
          "start": 88.2,
          "end": 90.44,
          "en": "which should be an empty string initially,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 29,
          "start": 90.44,
          "end": 93.84,
          "en": "and an entered text property,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 30,
          "start": 93.84,
          "end": 96.12299999999999,
          "en": "which also is an empty string initially.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 31,
          "start": 97.62,
          "end": 100.38,
          "en": "Back in the new ticket component template,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 32,
          "start": 100.38,
          "end": 104.49000000000001,
          "en": "we can then use NG model with that two-way binding syntax,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 33,
          "start": 104.49000000000001,
          "end": 106.17,
          "en": "which looks like this,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 34,
          "start": 106.17,
          "end": 110.098,
          "en": "square brackets around parentheses around NG model",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 35,
          "start": 110.098,
          "end": 114.36,
          "en": "to set and bind the entered title here",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 36,
          "start": 114.36,
          "end": 117.354,
          "en": "and do it on the text area",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 37,
          "start": 117.354,
          "end": 122.223,
          "en": "to set and bind the entered text.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 38,
          "start": 124.11,
          "end": 127.95,
          "en": "Now with that we can actually get rid of the parameters",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 39,
          "start": 127.95,
          "end": 132.54,
          "en": "that are passed to on submit and get rid of the title input",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 40,
          "start": 132.54,
          "end": 135.75,
          "en": "and text input template variables",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 41,
          "start": 135.75,
          "end": 138.93,
          "en": "because I'm now switching to using two-way binding",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 42,
          "start": 138.93,
          "end": 140.703,
          "en": "for getting that user input.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 43,
          "start": 141.87,
          "end": 144.72,
          "en": "So in the new ticket component TypeScript file,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 44,
          "start": 144.72,
          "end": 149.72,
          "en": "in on submit, we should no longer expect those parameters.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 45,
          "start": 150.301,
          "end": 153.72,
          "en": "And instead for emitting the add event,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 46,
          "start": 153.72,
          "end": 156.664,
          "en": "we now wanna reference entered title",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 47,
          "start": 156.664,
          "end": 159.423,
          "en": "and entered text here.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 48,
          "start": 160.335,
          "end": 163.2,
          "en": "With that, if you save everything,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 49,
          "start": 163.2,
          "end": 166.5,
          "en": "you should get the same behavior as before.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 50,
          "start": 166.5,
          "end": 168.48,
          "en": "I can submit these tickets",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 51,
          "start": 168.48,
          "end": 171.063,
          "en": "and everything works the way it did before.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 52,
          "start": 172.2,
          "end": 175.53,
          "en": "We could now also clear the form in a different way",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 53,
          "start": 175.53,
          "end": 178.77,
          "en": "because now instead of calling reset on the form,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 54,
          "start": 178.77,
          "end": 181.23,
          "en": "since I'm using two-way binding,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 55,
          "start": 181.23,
          "end": 183.09,
          "en": "which means I'm not just listening",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 56,
          "start": 183.09,
          "end": 184.86,
          "en": "to changes to those inputs,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 57,
          "start": 184.86,
          "end": 188.7,
          "en": "but I can also send new values back into them,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 58,
          "start": 188.7,
          "end": 193.29,
          "en": "we can clear both inputs by resetting entered title",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 59,
          "start": 193.29,
          "end": 195.64,
          "en": "and entered text back to empty strings",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 60,
          "start": 195.64,
          "end": 198.573,
          "en": "after we extracted their values.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 61,
          "start": 199.41,
          "end": 203.57999999999998,
          "en": "So here after calling emit, we can set entered title back",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 62,
          "start": 203.57999999999998,
          "end": 207.679,
          "en": "to an empty string and enter text back to an empty string.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 63,
          "start": 207.679,
          "end": 211.56,
          "en": "And by doing this thanks to two-Way binding,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 64,
          "start": 211.56,
          "end": 215.01,
          "en": "you'll see that the form will still be reset",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 65,
          "start": 215.01,
          "end": 217.07999999999998,
          "en": "because yeah, as mentioned,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 66,
          "start": 217.07999999999998,
          "end": 221.439,
          "en": "we're passing values back into those inputs.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 67,
          "start": 221.439,
          "end": 224.25,
          "en": "But that's of course nothing new.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 68,
          "start": 224.25,
          "end": 227.084,
          "en": "You did learn about two-way binding before.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 69,
          "start": 227.084,
          "end": 231.36,
          "en": "Now, however, we'll set up custom two-way binding",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 70,
          "start": 231.36,
          "end": 233.103,
          "en": "for our own component.",
          "zh": ""
        }
      ]
    }
  ],
  "errors": []
}
